PRIVATE REFLECTION: {The core evidence is the canonical order thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac-gal-str (increasing min). “Azi expressed long before any other tested marker” requires azi to be strictly proximal, i.e., oriT immediately adjacent to azi with transfer directed into the azi–leu–thr arc and a long empty arc before the next selectable marker.  

Only an origin placed near ton and polarized ton → azi satisfies both proximity and the observed temporal gap. That geometry is labeled “clockwise near ton” by the majority (A).  

Options that place oriT near thr necessarily mobilize leu before azi, violating the data; origins near lac/pro/str place azi far downstream. Colleague 1/8 therefore invert the polarity relative to the order. The clockwise/counterclockwise label is convention-dependent, but the relative geometry (ton-origin, azi-first) is unambiguous and matches A. No figure supplied, so reasoning rests solely on the established marker order and the definition of proximal marker.}

